  "name": null,
  "problem": "Find a parametric equation of the osculating plane for the curve  $r(t)$ at the point where $t=0,$ given that\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,T(0)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}⟨-1,-1,1⟩,\\,N(0)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨0,-1,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively.",
